          "We recommend checking the sentences below, and add any missing effect sizes.",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(c(\"gav, t(40) = 2.9, gav = 0.45.\", \"gz, t(40) = 2.9, g z = 0.45.\", \n\"grm, t(40) = 2.9, Hedges' grm = 0.45.\", \"gs, t(40) = 2.9, gs = 0.45.\", \n\"Hedges' g av, t(40) = 2.9, Hedges' g av = 0.45.\")), names = \"\", class = \"data.frame\", row.names = c(NA, \n-5L))\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 2, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "::: {.callout-tip title=\"Learn More\" collapse=\"true\"}\n\nFor metascientific articles demonstrating that effect sizes are often not reported:\n\n* Peng, C.-Y. J., Chen, L.-T., Chiang, H.-M., & Chiang, Y.-C. (2013). The Impact of APA and AERA Guidelines on Effect Size Reporting. Educational Psychology Review, 25(2), 157–209. doi:[10.1007/s10648-013-9218-2](https://doi.org/10.1007/s10648-013-9218-2).\n\nFor educational material on reporting effect sizes:\n\n* [Guide to Effect Sizes and Confidence Intervals](https://matthewbjane.quarto.pub/guide-to-effect-sizes-and-confidence-intervals/)\n\n:::\n",
          "::: {.callout-tip title=\"All detected and assessed stats\" collapse=\"true\"}\n\n\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(Sentence = c(\"gav, t(40) = 2.9, gav = 0.45.\", \n\"gz, t(40) = 2.9, g z = 0.45.\", \"grm, t(40) = 2.9, Hedges' grm = 0.45.\", \n\"gs, t(40) = 2.9, gs = 0.45.\", \"Hedges' g av, t(40) = 2.9, Hedges' g av = 0.45.\"\n), \"Effect Size\" = c(NA_character_, NA_character_, NA_character_, \nNA_character_, NA_character_), \"Reported Test\" = c(\"t(40) = 2.9\", \n\"t(40) = 2.9\", \"t(40) = 2.9\", \"t(40) = 2.9\", \"t(40) = 2.9\"), \n    \"Test Type\" = c(\"t-test\", \"t-test\", \"t-test\", \"t-test\", \"t-test\"\n    ), \"d Coherence\" = c(\"indeterminate\", \"indeterminate\", \"indeterminate\", \n    \"indeterminate\", \"indeterminate\"), \"d Assumption\" = c(\"none\", \n    \"none\", \"none\", \"none\", \"none\"), \"d Coherence Note\" = c(\"No parseable d effect size found.\", \n    \"No parseable d effect size found.\", \"No parseable d effect size found.\", \n    \"No parseable d effect size found.\", \"No parseable d effect size found.\"\n    ), \"eta Coherence\" = c(NA_character_, NA_character_, NA_character_, \n    NA_character_, NA_character_), \"eta Assumption\" = c(NA_character_, \n    NA_character_, NA_character_, NA_character_, NA_character_\n    ), \"eta Coherence Note\" = c(NA_character_, NA_character_, \n    NA_character_, NA_character_, NA_character_)), row.names = c(NA, \n-5L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 5, FALSE)\n```\n\n\n:::\n"
